<!--
     Time & Action calendars (garment.tna) — garment_tna. One TNA per order
     (order_tee / order_polo / order_hoodie, created in 03_order_demo.xml),
     each carrying its own Fabric Booking -> Fabric In-House -> Cutting ->
     Sewing -> Finishing -> Final Inspection -> Ex-Factory -> Shipment
     pipeline (garment.tna.activity for the work stages, garment.tna.milestone
     for the two closing checkpoint gates), dated to match the real
     order/shipment dates set in 03_order_demo.xml.

     Reused rather than duplicated: the knitwear TNA template shipped as seed
     data in garment_tna (data/garment_tna_template_data.xml,
     tna_template_knitwear_example) is referenced by ref on all three
     calendars — all three styles (tee/polo/hoodie) are knit/fleece per
     DEMO_STORY.md, so the knitwear example fits all of them; no woven
     template is used since none of the three styles is woven.

     Narrative: order_tee's fabric delivery from Delta Knit Fabrics
     (supplier_deltaknit / partner_deltaknit) arrives 8 days late (a mill
     yarn shortage) — logged as a High-severity garment.tna.delay on the
     "Fabric In-House" activity (flagged is_milestone) — and the factory
     recovers the slip with a compressed cutting/sewing schedule so the
     original shipment date is still met. order_polo and order_hoodie run
     to plan with no delays, to keep the delay-tracking showcase isolated
     to one clear example per DEMO_STORY.md's instructions.

     All three TNAs are dated Mar-Jul 2026 (already in the past relative to
     any later install), so status is set to 'closed' with every activity
     'completed' throughout, matching the shipped/closed-out orders they
     belong to.
-->
